    section.experience
      header
        h1(data-l10n-id="experience") Experience
      
      table
        tr
          td
            | 2024–
            span(data-l10n-id="present") Present
          td
            p.position Senior Software Engineer, DataSnipper
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_14")
              p Created and led the frontend guild, establishing frontend architecture, engineering standards and development practices. Built the frontend deployment platform and reusable infrastructure that take a new application from idea to a deployed, browser-testable environment in under 20 minutes.
              p Introduced agentic development practices: built a skills-based knowledge base from 100+ company repositories so agents can work beyond individual projects, and a workflow with up to five parallel agents on Git worktrees that cut development time on platform projects several times.
        tr
          td 2023–2024
          td
            p.position Staff Engineer, i3D.net
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_13")
              p i3D.net, a Ubisoft company, provides game hosting and global infrastructure for online games. I owned the frontend pillar: technical direction, coordination with other pillars, and support of the frontend engineers.
              p Defined the frontend architecture and infrastructure, introduced quality standards with processes to monitor and enforce them, and maintained the frontend roadmap. Created development paths and learning opportunities for engineers while staying hands-on with product work.
              p The result was a frontend platform and architectural standards that made it easier to add new applications and extend existing ones, including a dashboard for managing game hosting and deploying new games for enterprise customers and indie developers.
        tr
          td 2023–2024
          td
            p.position Head of Department, Projector Institute
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_15")
              p Helped build a frontend course lineup covering HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and React.js. Developed the processes for creating and maintaining courses from the ground up, including calculating and visualising teaching workload, preparing new courses for launch, and coordinating authors and teachers.
        tr
          td 2021–2023
          td
            p.position Senior Software Engineer, Amazon Web Services (AWS)
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_12")
              p Owned the frontend for the RDS Ops Console — the internal control plane AWS engineers use to operate Amazon RDS. Defined the frontend roadmap, including migrating the console from a legacy Ruby and jQuery stack to React and TypeScript, introduced code quality controls and a unit testing system with coverage enforcement, and built feedback mechanisms to surface UI/UX issues reported by console users. These improvements doubled (2×) the console's internal user satisfaction score. Also introduced canary testing across the console, giving the team confidence that critical functionality was working and letting us catch issues before they reached users.
        tr
          td 2019–2021
          td
            p.position Senior Frontend Developer,
              |  
              a(href="https://werkspot.nl/") Werkspot
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_11")
              p Worked as a Frontend Developer at Werkspot, helping build and roll out a new frontend stack based on React and Next.js while migrating the existing application to the new architecture.
              p Developed key parts of the frontend platform, including the translation and form management systems, and introduced a grid layout system. Contributed to business-critical user flows and helped establish the technical foundations for the new frontend stack.
              p Also contributed to hiring and represented the company at conferences and through technical articles, helping strengthen the company’s engineering brand.
        tr
          td 2017–2018
          td
            p.position Lead Frontend Developer,
              |  
              a(href="https://www.templatemonster.com/") TemplateMonster.com
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_10")
              p Led three frontend teams of eight engineers across Lviv, Mykolaiv, and Kyiv, with responsibility for hiring, mentoring, technical direction, and day-to-day engineering leadership.
              p Played a key role in transforming the product from a marketplace for TemplateMonster-created products into a platform where anyone could sell digital media content. Contributed to the architecture and frontend technical direction of the new platform, which was built from the ground up around a new design system and more than 40 REST microservices.
              p Established the frontend architecture and development practices for the new platform, including a custom React-based SSR solution. Led major performance optimisation efforts, including HTTP/2 Server Push and client-side caching, to ensure the platform could scale with the new product model.
        tr
          td 2016–2017
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer,
              |  
              a(href="http://www.vaimo.com/") Vaimo
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_9")
              p Built Magento storefronts for Brown-Forman (Jack Daniel's), Bauhaus Sweden, Ontime and Alyasra.
        tr
          td 2015–2016
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer,
              |  
              a(href="https://www.aretodev.com/") Areto Development
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_8")
              p Worked as a Frontend Developer on projects for Areto Development, Vacay Kit, 3 Way Talk and Yoke Labs.
        tr
          td 2014–2015
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer,
              |  
              a(href="http://www.alignedcode.com/") Aligned Code
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_7")
              p Worked as a Frontend Developer on projects for Aligned Code, Binary Garage, Yoke Labs and CB Territory.
        tr
          td 2013–2016
          td
            p.position Editor in Chief, Founder, Frontender Magazine
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_16")
              p Frontender Magazine was a free online publication about frontend development for Russian-speaking developers. I organised the work of the editors, six core-team translators, and 15 freelance translators, overseeing the translation and publication of around 300 articles. At its peak, the magazine reached more than 100,000 unique users per month.
              p I built the platform from the ground up, with extensive automation for content acquisition and publishing. This included analysing email subscriptions to discover new articles, extracting article content from websites, providing automated translation hints, generating static content, automatically requesting translation permissions from authors, and other tools that streamlined the editorial workflow.
        tr
          td 2012–2013
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer, Parallels
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_6")
              p Built the frontend of Focal Point, a home office product for small businesses.
        tr
          td 2012
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer, Giftofoni
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_5")
              p Built the frontend of Giftofoni.
        tr
          td 2011–2012
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer, ZN.UA
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_4")
              p Frontend development for ZN.UA (a leading Ukrainian news outlet) and Znaki.fm, including complex editorial and campaign-driven experiences.
              p Built sophisticated landing pages for advertising campaigns on ZN.UA, as well as custom-designed pages for major journalistic investigations, combining bespoke layouts, interactive elements, and infographics to present complex content clearly.
        tr
          td 2011
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer,
              |  
              a(href="http://evilmartians.com/") Evil Martians
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_3")
              p Worked with the Evil Martians studio as a Frontend Developer on projects including Groupon Russia and i-lift.tv.
        tr
          td 2010–2011
          td
            p.position Frontend Developer, Pokeroff
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_2")
              p Development of the Pokeroff.ru portal from the ground up, including frontend architecture and implementation, as well as designing and setting up the build system.
        tr
          td 2000–2010
          td
            p.position Software Engineer, R.A.M.
            div(data-l10n-id="experience_1")
              p Development of digital projects for advertising agencies R.A.M. and Paradigm Consulting Group, working with brands such as Pall Mall, Kent, Camel, Lay’s, Kinder, DreamWorks, MTV, Indesit, Samsung, and others.
              p Provided services as a Frontend Developer, Flash Developer, and Designer, covering UI design, illustration, animation, ActionScript development, and frontend implementation.

